  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "The intense tension between Chef Barinov and his boss Igor Valentinovich continues to grow in the busy kitchen. The chef deliberately asks the frustrated boss to serve him another cup of tea, trying to test the man's patience and show who is really in charge.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мой чай уже закончился.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А, налей-ка мне чашечку.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "А, он закончился.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Я сейчас скажу, вам принесут.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Шеф, еще чаек.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Поражаюсь вам, Виктор Петрович.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Как у вас все схвачено.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Стоило только подумать, вот пожалуйста.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ой, остыл совсем, я свежий заварю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Ничего страшного.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Я не люблю горячего.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Как хотите, Игорь Валентинович.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А я люблю горячий чай.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let us break down this interaction.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А, налей-ка мне чашечку.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Oh, pour me a cup, would you?' Russian leaves out 'am', 'is', or 'are' in the present tense, linking 'pour' straight to 'small cup'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "А, он закончился.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Oh, it is gone.' Notice the reflexive ending on the verb for 'ended', which directs the action back onto the subject.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Я сейчас скажу, вам принесут.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will ask them to bring some.' The character combines 'I' with 'will bring' in a natural Russian turn of phrase.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Шеф, еще чаек.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Boss, more tea.' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'chef' with 'tea'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Поражаюсь вам, Виктор Петрович.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I have to hand it to you, Viktor Petrovich.' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'be amazed' with 'Petrovich'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Как у вас все схвачено.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You have got everything under control.' Notice how 'how' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'under control'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Стоило только подумать, вот пожалуйста.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You only had to think of it, and there it was.' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'to cost' with 'please'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ой, остыл совсем, я свежий заварю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Oh, it has gone cold. I will brew a fresh pot.' Chef Viktor combines 'oh' with 'brew' in a natural Russian turn of phrase.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Ничего страшного.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'That is all right.' The character combines 'nothing' with 'terrible' in a natural Russian turn of phrase.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Я не люблю горячего.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I do not like it hot.' The negative particle sits directly before the verb for 'love' to negate the action. Now let us listen to the conversation again without interruption.",
      "gap": 0.9
